  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1222 PM MDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nThe Monsoon high will move back southeast to over west central NM\nand weaken to near 595dam at 500mb from Saturday into Sunday. A\nmoderate to major heat risk will continue for much of the area and\nmore Heat Advisories will likely be required for the Northwest\nPlateau and middle RGV. Daytime heating initiated convection that\ndevelops this weekend will continue to favor strong/erratic wind\ngusts over soaking rains, except for over the southern mountains\nwhere more efficient rain-making is likely due to a higher PWAT\natmosphere. The forecast trends next week will be for decreasing \nheat impacts and increasing thunderstorm impacts as the Monsoon \nhigh weakens further and moves slowly east to into TX.",
